            {"title": "A whole mini-RAG in plain Python (toy embeddings, extractive answer)", "language": "python", "runnable": True,
             "code": "import math, re\n\nDOCS = {\n    'leave.txt': 'Employees get 25 days of annual leave. Parental leave is 26 weeks for the primary caregiver.',\n    'expenses.txt': 'Expense reports must be filed within 30 days. Travel above 500 dollars needs manager approval.',\n}\n\ndef words(text):\n    return re.findall(r'[a-z0-9]+', text.lower())\n\n# 1. index: split into sentences (our 'chunks') and embed each (word counts)\nchunks = []\nfor name, text in DOCS.items():\n    for sentence in re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text):\n        chunks.append((name, sentence))\nVOCAB = sorted({w for _, s in chunks for w in words(s)})\n\ndef embed(text):\n    ws = words(text)\n    return [ws.count(w) for w in VOCAB]\n\ndef cosine(a, b):\n    d = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))\n    n = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a)) * math.sqrt(sum(y * y for y in b))\n    return d / n if n else 0.0\n\nindex = [(name, s, embed(s)) for name, s in chunks]\n\n# 2. retrieve\nquestion = 'How long is parental leave?'\nq = embed(question)\nranked = sorted(index, key=lambda c: -cosine(q, c[2]))[:2]\n\n# 3. build a grounded prompt with numbered sources\nsources = '\\n'.join(f'[{i}] ({name}) {s}' for i, (name, s, _) in enumerate(ranked, 1))\nprompt = f'Answer ONLY from the sources and cite them like [1]. If they do not contain the answer, say so.\\n\\nSources:\\n{sources}\\n\\nQuestion: {question}'\nprint(prompt)\n",
             "expected_output": "Answer ONLY from the sources and cite them like [1]. If they do not contain the answer, say so.\n\nSources:\n[1] (leave.txt) Parental leave is 26 weeks for the primary caregiver.\n[2] (leave.txt) Employees get 25 days of annual leave.\n\nQuestion: How long is parental leave?",
             "explain": [{"lines": "3-6", "text": "Two small 'documents'."}, {"lines": "11-16", "text": "Indexing: cut documents into sentence-sized chunks and remember which file each came from."}, {"lines": "18-30", "text": "Toy embeddings and cosine similarity (real systems use a learned embedding model, see the Embeddings lessons)."}, {"lines": "32-35", "text": "Retrieval: embed the question and take the 2 most similar chunks."}, {"lines": "37-40", "text": "The grounded prompt: rules, numbered sources, then the question. This text is what you would send to the model; the model's reply would cite [1]."}]},
